  "slug": "learning-causation-2f3a",
  "summary": "SigDoTS and ProClust add null-model testing to domain and cell-group calls, while benchmarks probe sequencing-depth and network-estimation limits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is replacing heuristic partitioning with statistically tested outputs. SigDoTS adds hypothesis testing with FWER control to spatial transcriptomics domain detection, merging or retaining candidate domains based on null simulations. ProClust tests scRNA-seq cluster significance, merging overclustered groups via log-concave cluster modelling and projection-based tests. CellSavior applies confidence-weighted merging within ensemble clustering for targeted scDNA-seq cell calling, matching CellFinder in 31 of 33 datasets. Related work pairs explicit probabilistic or null models with standardization: MAUDE-Py adds automated baselines and null sampling for sorting-based CRISPR screens, and bsseq gains a read-based likelihood framework for sample-specific CpG loci in long-read data. Benchmarks define where current practice falls short: typical RNA-seq depths miss alternative splicing, precision-matrix estimators for differential co-expression are compared systematically, and SigBridgeR unifies eight phenotype-associated subpopulation algorithms. Tool modernization items (deepTools4, CLIPittyClip) and an oyster genome assembly sit outside this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
